An excellent game, my best yet. A female wizard, XL22, -42 AC, about
309 HP and 320 Pow. +4 Magicbane, +7 Fire Brand, +7 Werebane, the Eye
of Mispelling and the Orb of Fate (from a Valk bones) got me through to
the endgame. Before killing Rodney for the Book I switched from a
shield of reflection to an amulet of reflection, to improve
spellcasting. Killed Rodney, performed the ritual, saw Moloch's Sanctum
for the very first time outside of wizmode. Got the amulet, climbed all
the way back to DL1. Some preparation, very nervous, never did the
planes before.  One important thing I forgot was some way to detect the
portals.

So I fought through the planes of Earth and Air with some difficulty
but no real scares, and was wandering around Fire looking for the
portal. A captain runs up to me on that level, tries to switch from his
cursed crossbow to a cockatrice corpse (!) but can't. After I kill him,
I take off my ring of levitation to wield his cockatrice corpse.
Discover it doesn't work against Xorns or Fire elementals, who seem to
be bothering me the most, so I switch back to Magicbane. Forgot I was
no longer wearing my ring of levitation....

Didn't get to see the actual death message because I had my finger on
space -- so many pets fighting so many fire elementals. (Charm Monster
from a spellbook, with INT 22, at 0% failure, totally rocks!!  Only
problem was I kept using up my POW.)

